indow adoption trap** (productivity/adoption % must always carry `window` + `sample_size`, never a bare %).\n\n**Six serial waves (each with done-when + Given/Then specs)**\n- **W1** â€” Read-only scaffold + data layer + serving shell: `dashboard/` package, `ro_connect`, freshness fingerprint, blueprint factory (`/api/health`, `/api/fingerprint`, `/api/state`), Flask app, HTML/CSS/JS shell with \"as of\" stamp + fingerprint poll. Proves read-only enforcement + embeddability boundary.\n- **W2** â€” Morning glance panel: `reports.py` readers for `latest_summary.json` (productivity_index, costs MTD, finds/top_finds, noise_audit, badges), briefing note, latest weekly; `/api/morning`; top-finds cards, adoption line with window+sample_size, cost rollup. Fails soft on missing files.\n- **W3** â€” Errors/health panel: `health.py` (`run_status` w/ critic_c degrade, `noise_audit` w/ offending rows, `backfill_audits`, `recent_rejects`, allowlisted `sweep_log_tail`); `/api/health` + `/api/health/detail?signal=`; signals expand in-page (G3).\n- **W4** â€” \"What was new\" per-sweep browser: `list_sweep_dates`/`read_sweep` (allowlisted to `reports/<kind>/`); `/api/sweeps` + `/api/sweep/<kind>/<date>`; kindÃ—date selector linked from morning finds-new counts.\n- **W5** â€” Catalog taxonomy map (G1 v1): `catalog.py` `taxonomy_map()` (non-retired `artifacts` LEFT JOIN `embeddings` by kindÃ—domain_path, NULLâ†’\"unclassified\", taste + dead-link/stars overlay from `link_health`) + `artifacts_in()`; `map.js` D3 sunburst reusing `library/_map.html` idiom; click-to-filter.\n- **W6** â€” Polish + embeddability proof + docs: global \"as of\" header, audited empty/error states, `DASHBOARD.md` with exact Anchor-tab mount steps, integration test mounting blueprint on a second bare Flask app exercising all `/api/*`, live read-only smoke (mtimes unchanged), and a **deferred** force-directed knowledge-graph note (sources: shared `domain_path`, `github_network_parent`, `prov_edges`, `hh_events`) â€” named, not built.\n\n**Grounding caveats noted in the plan itself**\n- Data contract grounded in `kb/schema.sql` + live `reports/` surfaces as of **2026-06-11**; cited live-KB row counts are snapshots that drift, so every query resolves its set by rule, not by hardcoded count.\n\nWant me to save this as an Aurora memory (e.g. `foreman-handoff-dashboard.md` + a MEMORY.md pointer), or is this summary for in-session use only?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7061,"cache_read_input_tokens":33565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7061},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aade9690-024d-45d0-b824-77fa426de17d","uuid":"35bc0771-b00c-4c6c-bcb5-46548571cf25","request_id":"req_011CcBopoTf47E6VqUMLRYDB"}
